?TACL ROUTINE
== dow: the day of the week for a timestamp, or for right now.
== Straight from section 4 of the TACL Reference Manual, which is
== where most people meet their first routine.
#FRAME
#PUSH days timestamp rslt
#SET rslt [#ARGUMENT /VALUE timestamp/ NUMBER END]
[#CASE [rslt]
  |1| SINK [#ARGUMENT END]
  |2| #SET timestamp [#TIMESTAMP]
]
#SET days [#COMPUTE [timestamp] / (24 * 60 * 60 * 100)]
#SET days [#COMPUTE days - ((days / 7) * 7)]
#RESULT [#CASE [days]
  |0| Tuesday
  |1| Wednesday
  |2| Thursday
  |3| Friday
  |4| Saturday
  |5| Sunday
  |OTHERWISE| Monday
]
#UNFRAME
